{"id":"68c664e15b23a84c","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-thm-wadge-hierarchy.md","title":"Wadge Hierarchy","display":"thm-wadge-hierarchy — Wadge Hierarchy","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-wadge-hierarchy","aliases":["58-thm-wadge-hierarchy","Wadge Hierarchy","Wadge Order","Wadge Degrees"],"display":"thm-wadge-hierarchy — Wadge Hierarchy","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-thm-determinacy.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-wadge-hierarchy"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-wadge-hierarchy</span><span>Wadge Hierarchy</span><span>Wadge Order</span><span>Wadge Degrees</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-wadge-hierarchy — Wadge Hierarchy"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"db916f1fec757e0b\" href=\"?note=db916f1fec757e0b\" title=\"../batch02/58-thm-determinacy.md\">../batch02/58-thm-determinacy.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"44867449c3df728b\" href=\"?note=44867449c3df728b\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md\">../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega\">\\(\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega\\)</span> with its standard topology <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathcal N}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B,C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\">\\(A,B,C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\\)</span> (continuous-map predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_{\\mathrm I}=\\{s\\in\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}:|\\operatorname{dom}(s)|\\text{ is even}\\}\">\\(P_{\\mathrm I}=\\{s\\in\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}:|\\operatorname{dom}(s)|\\text{ is even}\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_{\\mathrm{II}}=\\{s\\in\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}:|\\operatorname{dom}(s)|\\text{ is odd}\\}\">\\(P_{\\mathrm{II}}=\\{s\\in\\omega^{&lt;\\omega}:|\\operatorname{dom}(s)|\\text{ is odd}\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\\)</span> are the predicates from the dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Determined}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Determined}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S\\)</span> are defined below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Determined}_S(C)\\leftrightarrow C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\land\\Bigl[\n&amp;\\exists\\sigma\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\sigma,P_{\\mathrm I},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathcal N\\;\n(\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x(2n)=\\sigma(x\\upharpoonright2n))\\to x\\in C)\\bigr)\\\\\n\\lor{}&amp;\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\tau,P_{\\mathrm{II}},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathcal N\\;\n(\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x(2n+1)=\\tau(x\\upharpoonright(2n+1)))\\to x\\notin C)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Determined}_S(C)\\leftrightarrow C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\land\\Bigl[\n&amp;\\exists\\sigma\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\sigma,P_{\\mathrm I},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathcal N\\;\n(\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x(2n)=\\sigma(x\\upharpoonright2n))\\to x\\in C)\\bigr)\\\\\n\\lor{}&amp;\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\tau,P_{\\mathrm{II}},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathcal N\\;\n(\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x(2n+1)=\\tau(x\\upharpoonright(2n+1)))\\to x\\notin C)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(A,B)\n\\leftrightarrow\nA,B\\subseteq\\mathcal N\n\\land\n\\exists f\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\n(f,\\mathcal N,\\tau_{\\mathcal N},\\mathcal N,\\tau_{\\mathcal N})\n\\land\nA=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:f(x)\\in B\\}\n\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(A,B)\n\\leftrightarrow\nA,B\\subseteq\\mathcal N\n\\land\n\\exists f\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\n(f,\\mathcal N,\\tau_{\\mathcal N},\\mathcal N,\\tau_{\\mathcal N})\n\\land\nA=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:f(x)\\in B\\}\n\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}wadge\\text{-}hierarchy} \\vdash\nA,B\\subseteq\\mathcal N\n\\land\\forall C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\;\\mathrm{Determined}_S(C)\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(A,B)\n\\lor\n\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(\\mathcal N\\setminus B,A)\n\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}wadge\\text{-}hierarchy} \\vdash\nA,B\\subseteq\\mathcal N\n\\land\\forall C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\;\\mathrm{Determined}_S(C)\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(A,B)\n\\lor\n\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(\\mathcal N\\setminus B,A)\n\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Wadge (1970s): introduced reduction order.</li>\n<li>The determinacy assumption is expanded into a set-coded winning strategy for one of the two players; it is not an undefined game predicate.</li>\n<li>Key: determinacy makes Wadge order well-behaved.</li>\n<li>Under AD, Wadge degrees are essentially linearly ordered up to complement and the order is well-founded.</li>\n<li>For Borel sets, the hierarchy aligns with classical Borel rank complexity.</li>\n<li>Without determinacy, the displayed semilinearity and global well-foundedness can fail.</li>\n<li>Applications: descriptive set theory, computational complexity analogues.</li>\n<li>Wadge hierarchy: &quot;degrees of unsolvability&quot; for sets of reals.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-thm-determinacy.md","status":"resolved","id":"db916f1fec757e0b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-thm-determinacy.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"44867449c3df728b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal N=\\omega^\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathcal N}","display":false},{"tex":"A,B,C\\subseteq\\mathcal N","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S","display":false},{"tex":"P_{\\mathrm I}=\\{s\\in\\omega^{<\\omega}:|\\operatorname{dom}(s)|\\text{ is even}\\}","display":false},{"tex":"P_{\\mathrm{II}}=\\{s\\in\\omega^{<\\omega}:|\\operatorname{dom}(s)|\\text{ is odd}\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Determined}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Determined}_S(C)\\leftrightarrow C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\land\\Bigl[\n&\\exists\\sigma\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\sigma,P_{\\mathrm I},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathcal N\\;\n(\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x(2n)=\\sigma(x\\upharpoonright2n))\\to x\\in C)\\bigr)\\\\\n\\lor{}&\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\tau,P_{\\mathrm{II}},\\omega)\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathcal N\\;\n(\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x(2n+1)=\\tau(x\\upharpoonright(2n+1)))\\to x\\notin C)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(A,B)\n\\leftrightarrow\nA,B\\subseteq\\mathcal N\n\\land\n\\exists f\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\n(f,\\mathcal N,\\tau_{\\mathcal N},\\mathcal N,\\tau_{\\mathcal N})\n\\land\nA=\\{x\\in\\mathcal N:f(x)\\in B\\}\n\\right].","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}wadge\\text{-}hierarchy} \\vdash\nA,B\\subseteq\\mathcal N\n\\land\\forall C\\subseteq\\mathcal N\\;\\mathrm{Determined}_S(C)\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(A,B)\n\\lor\n\\mathrm{WadgeLeq}_S(\\mathcal N\\setminus B,A)\n\\right].","display":true}],"bytes":2610,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4482","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-thm-wadge-hierarchy.md|58-thm-wadge-hierarchy]]（batch04）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-280","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equa